## Architecture Overview

### **Data Sources**
- **CRM System**: Customer Relationship Management data (CSV files)
- **ERP System**: Enterprise Resource Planning data (CSV files)
- **SQL Server**: Primary data source

### **Data Warehouse Layers**

#### **1. Bronze Layer** (Raw Data)
- **Purpose**: Store raw, unprocessed data from all sources
- **Object Type**: Tables
- **Load Strategy**: 
  - Batch Processing
  - Full Load
  - Truncate & Insert
- **Transformations**: None
- **Data Model**: As-is (None)

#### **2. Silver Layer** (Cleaned & Standardized)
- **Purpose**: Store cleaned and standardized data
- **Object Type**: Tables
- **Load Strategy**:
  - Batch Processing
  - Insert Only
  - Bulk Upsert
- **Transformations**:
  - Data Cleansing
  - Data Standardization
  - Data Normalization
  - Derived Columns
  - Data Enrichment
- **Data Model**: As-is (None)

#### **3. Gold Layer** (Business-Ready Data)
- **Purpose**: Refined, aggregated data ready for consumption
- **Object Type**: Views
- **Load Strategy**: No Direct Load (derived from Silver Layer)
- **Transformations**:
  - Data Integration
  - Aggregations
  - Business Logics
- **Data Model**:
  - Star Schema
  - Flat Tables
  - Aggregated Tables

### **Consumers**
- **BI & Reporting**: Business Intelligence and analytics tools
- **Machine Learning**: ML models for predictive analytics
